          "explanation": "Both Newton (container) and Leibniz (relations) treat space and time as mind-independent. Kant's distinctive move is treating them as pure forms of intuition — necessary structures the mind itself supplies as the condition for having any spatial or temporal experience, explaining geometry's a priori certainty.",
