          "explanation": "The popular 'thesis-antithesis-synthesis' triad is a simplification later applied to Hegel, tracing more to Fichte and to popularizing textbooks, not Hegel's own precise vocabulary. Hegel's own terms are immediate/abstract position, negation, and the negation of the negation, captured by his term Aufhebung, or sublation.",
